joining us now from greater southeast  energy hub is peter goody  and thank you for that introduction and  thank you to babe and mitch suffolk and  to all their sponsors for uh organizing  this event today i think it's a great  opportunity to get a focus on business  and a relationship built around how we  take forward  uh suffolk on its net zero journey  before i start and signpost some of the  things that are going on  in  suffolk to support businesses i'd just  like to give you one word and that word  is momentum  now momentum  it's about impetus  moving a body  me  yourself in the audience your businesses  the local authorities ipswich suffolk  the uk the global community we all need  momentum on this zero carbon journey  i think about covid  and i think the couple of things that  covid pandemic has taught me  the first one is around  how important good science is and  secondly how we apply  innovation from that good science the  second thing it's taught me is around  people and how people take that  innovation and that solution  to solve things now we can do that we've  shown that over the last two years  and the zero carbon journey  is a similar thing that we need to get  both  impetus and our bodies moving  so we need momentum  i don't flatter myself that i'm i've got  any more insight to add to the room  and the people that are in this room  today although uh i do have uh some  knowledge of the work that's being gone  going on in suffolk over the last 20  years  but i think back to 1992 in the rio  earth summit  which was the starting point of some of  this momentum  the conference of parties cop  which was initiated following the rio  earth summit in 1992  is now at its latest stage  next month with cop 26 in glasgow  and i look out into the room and i ask  you and i urge you  to use this event  and to use cop26 to give us momentum on  this zero carbon journey so that's my  speechy firing over i move on to the  the really important bits that i'd like  to cover with you today which around the  services available to businesses  whether they're businesses looking to  become more energy efficient  or looking to invest and generate their  own energy  or whether they're businesses that want  to develop the goods the services and  the skills that we need  to move on this zero carbon journey in  suffolk  so  i'm going to name check some  organizations in their own room today  but it's your job not mine to go and  meet them  to talk to them today  to visit their websites to get to phone  them and find out the things that you  need whether you're a small medium-sized  business whether you're a local  authority whether you're even an  individual consumer  get the information you need today to  get that momentum  so that we can move forward so that's my  challenge to you i will be endeavoring  to talk to those organizations as well  and i look forward to those  conversations over the next  four to six hours as long as we we get  to that point today and we will  benefit all that knowledge that we got  in the room  so if i may  uh  i don't know whether the slides are  moving but i'll leave the slides it's  fine um  these are sort of questions that  some of the businesses i've been talking  to  have put to me and i talked to some of  the energy advisors that are here today  that have been supporting local  businesses  the first thing is i don't know what to  do as a small business i i'm too busy  i'm too stressed i've got to keep my  business going  um i'm not  got the time or i don't know where to go  for the information  also is there money available can i get  a grant  now these things  are potentially questions that we can  answer today  thank you  apologies  yeah thank you  so that help is at hand  and hopefully today  we can flag  up the opportunities that are available  to businesses in the location  so to start  if you're a small and medium-sized  business you may think you haven't  started on this journey but you already  have you've just been doing it as good  business practice  a couple of examples of businesses that  i know one was a garage services  servicing cars when the cars come in  they might replace a tyre for the mot  they then decided well while they  replace the tire could we not get the  equipment in to be able to repair that  tyre  so they provide an additional service to  that business to that customer  by changing their business model and  adding something to their business but  they reduce their environmental cost by  reducing waste of throwing that tyre  away they did it as good business  practice they didn't do it because it  was an environmental thing it saved them  money and gave their customer a better  better service second example  is a small business  their roof was leaking so they had  somebody come in  replace their roof but they insulated it  they weren't going to do it but they  decided yeah we'll insulate it  their employees  were so happy with that one action that  business took because it improved the  space they were working in the winter  time when it was cold before it was  warmer and in the summer time it was too  hot so it could kept the building cooler  so two very simple things they weren't  done for environmental reasons they  saved energy they reduced waste but what  they did do was benefit that business in  terms of its  customers  and its employees  now  we're going to focus on two things  um  that really other i would argue the end  point  in terms of benefit  and that's recognition  it's really important that we recognize  good practice  i never  feel comfortable with the word best  practice because that suggests you've  achieved the pinnacle we need to keep  moving on keep that momentum going but  good practice should be recognized and  in suffolk we're blessed  we have a carbon charter  which recognizes businesses that are on  this journey towards zero carbon  and any business that is following that  pathway  can choose to be part of that journey  using the carbon charity as a means of  recognition for their action and to  improve their brand awareness  and to show to their customers and  supply chain that they're serious about  becoming zero carbon  i'm just going to name check  a few businesses  have got calm childhood status  i could go on more than  more than uh you want me to but abc  taxes hold a tree anglia print barn  world print co-op  comes up a dozen or so times in terms of  the actions they've taken in terms of  suffolk carbon charter and taking action  james white drinks lignacite lindsey  lodge farm maple farm midas uk i could  go on and on and i'm sure you don't want  me to but this is a demonstration that  this is not something novel this is  something that businesses are getting on  with  and if you want to be on that journey  and you want that momentum  then the suffolk carbon charter is a way  of demonstrating that and recognizing it  we're really blessed that we're into the  second decade of the creating the  greenest county awards which recognizes  sustainability in the round  it recognizes that households businesses  communities are taking action and  we're blessed that they give  the opportunity for them to have a goal  of evening and some promotion  in suffolk about the things they're  doing so suffolk lagunas county i think  the deadline if you want to get your  nominations is close to play today  i can see some nodding so if you think  you've done some really good work get  your nomination in if you can think of a  business that's done some really good  work get your nomination in  and that would be something that will  give that business all that organization  whether it's community organization  recognition and reward for the good work  now taking a step back  i'd like you  to benefit today from the support that's  in the room not only from some of the  suppliers that are here and thank you  for coming along but two schemes that  are very worthwhile for small and  medium-sized enterprises to get involved  in  the first is the business energy  efficiency anglia scheme b for short  and  i hope one of the advisors will stick  their hand in the air  excellent  go see that gentleman if you're a small  or medium-sized enterprise and you want  to find out how to improve your carbon  footprint your environmental journey  get some momentum onto your improvements  find out about their or their auditing  and their independence and value that  they can add to your business find out  about the grants that they offer you  and get involved and participate and get  supported  the second is eastern new energy  are they in the room today  excellent hi joe  fantastic new scheme providing similar  range of services but if you're say on a  business park or an industrial trading  estate talk to them  they provide  access to expertise and independent  advice  and there's also grants available as  well  they will also support you if you've got  a product or a service that you want to  develop that is a green product  it's an environmental product it's a  product that will help reduce the  environmental impact of an organization  so talk about them about how you could  get your product to market  and i'm sure they can support you  i'm really pleased to be able to name  check those two organizations in  particular  but also talk to the suppliers whether  it's around led lighting boiler  replacement with  heat pumps or any other decarbonized  technology whether it's about insulation  whether it's about  system controls building controls  whether it's around changing motors  in your factory or process equipment  upgrades whether it's installing solar  power  all of these things can be achieved  they may require investment but some of  them are low and no cost options that  will add value to your business  now  i'd like also to finally look at  travel and mobility now if you go onto  the green suffolk website is a great  resource whether you're a householder  community business or otherwise  but go through that website and if your  customers or your employees come to your  your business premises  find out how they can come to your  business permit sustainably  you'll find on the um the greenish  county web the the green suffolk website  uh a web page called suffolk way to go  that will help you identify  walking maps routes for your staff to  walk to work cycle maps  schemes to help link up public transport  provision to allow you and your  customers to get you to your business  and for you to trade in a more  sustainable  way the other area was around  vehicles and particularly with the last  two years we've seen the rise of  home delivery  a lot of vans on the street we've also  heard about the  merging  policy positions around electrification  of passenger vehicles  with  new internal combustion engine sales  being prohibited from 2030  that raises the question around  infrastructure and charging  go and talk to peter here in terms of ev  charging  if you're a business  and you haven't got the capital  peter has it  it's a rental scheme two pounds a day  you can get an install  of an ev charging provision p i probably  dropped you in it you've probably got no  money whatsoever but anyway we'll do  that  use that scheme  to be able to get charging provision  into your business whether it's for your  own passenger vehicles or your white van  you'll be able to not only  charge your vehicle  but deliver savings into your business  okay the capital cost is the biggest  challenge i would argue with regard to  electrification of transportation we can  talk about range anxiety and we can talk  about all of the other issues but it's  the capital  to get you into that place now if we can  make it easier for businesses to get  into that  with no and low-cost capital routes  then hopefully that journey for that  business will be easier giving them  momentum to be able to move into an  electrified transport world  so talk to peter plug in suffolk  and i think with that i've probably name  checked as many as i can think of i'm  sure there are loads more out there but  please network talk to people not today  only but beyond this take it out talk to  your suppliers talk to your customers  find out who else out there wants to go  on that journey and give them momentum  as well  with that thank you  [Applause]  you

